oter frustration if the Democratic-led House  struggles with legislative compromise or internal party divisions .\n\u2022 The \"First 100 Hours\" Counter-Narrative: Republicans can use committee hearings, investigations , and public messaging to challenge Democratic policies on taxes, energy, tariffs, and foreign policy  (such as the handling of the war in Iran) .\nDefending and Flipping Swing Districts\n\u2022 Targeting Razor-Thin Margins: Control of the House typically comes down to a small number of competitive \"toss-up\" districts across key battleground states (such as Arizona, Pennsylvania, Michigan, Ohio, and Iowa) \n\u2022 Incumbency Advantage: Surviving Democratic incumbents will enter 2028 with structural name recognition and fundraising networks, meaning Republicans must aggressively recruit strong local candidates early and fund competitive challenger operations.\n\u2022 Nationalized vs. Local Issues: GOP candidates will need to localize races by tying Democratic opponents to national economic conditions , inflation, and cost-of-living pressures\n", "author": "Toobigtorig1234", "created": 1793813759325, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "Crlsniper", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Patriots we will win back the house and the senate 2028...Game face and game plan...Just because they won did not mean they will succeed..", "last_comment_created": 1793818906786, "content": "<p>Capitalizing on Midterm Overswing &amp; Voter Pendulum\n\u2022 Midterm Backlash Dynamic: Historically, the party in power in the White House often faces headwinds or overreach. Republicans will look to channel voter frustration if the Democratic-led House  struggles with legislative compromise or internal party divisions .\n\u2022 The &quot;First 100 Hours&quot; Counter-Narrative: Republicans can use committee hearings, investigations , and public messaging to challenge Democratic policies on taxes, energy, tariffs, and foreign policy  (such as the handling of the war in Iran) .\nDefending and Flipping Swing Districts\n\u2022 Targeting Razor-Thin Margins: Control of the House typically comes down to a small number of competitive &quot;toss-up&quot; districts across key battleground states (such as Arizona, Pennsylvania, Michigan, Ohio, and Iowa)\n\u2022 Incumbency Advantage: Surviving Democratic incumbents will enter 2028 with structural name recognition and fundraising networks, meaning Republicans must aggressively recruit strong local candidates early and fund competitive challenger operations.\n\u2022 Nationalized vs. Local Issues: GOP candidates will need to localize races by tying Democratic opponents to national economic conditions , inflation, and cost-of-living pressures</p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 8, "score_up": 23, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "2117773880769077666", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1AToYu8idH", "is_twitter": true, "is_admin": false, "score": 522, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8920233, "raw_content": "", "author": "PiratePatriotParrot", "created": 1793752560817, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "keeman", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "twitter.com", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1AToYu8idH.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://twitter.com/TONYxTWO/status/2117773